  "body": "Part 1 of 2 for #3098. This change records which control a machine has. The post in #3182 will use these facts to select a supported dialect.\n\n- A machine can state its control model, exact NC software release, installed options and tool-change procedure. An omitted option list means the options are unknown.\n- The machine sheet, saved project and post interface retain these facts. Existing machine files can omit them.\n- The Picomax 55 definition describes three-axis CNC operation with W fixed, NC software `340490-03` and manual tool changes. It leaves the absolute travel limits and installed software options unspecified.\n- A machine definition that also contains conflicting script inputs gets a diagnostic. This preserves explicit restrictions such as `rigidTapping: false`.\n\n### Evidence and outstanding checks\n\nThe target manual describes the retract in §7.4, p. 303 and the preset in §8.9, p. 492. The retract uses the active travel limit. Cycle 247 does not activate a preset in Test Run. [HEIDENHAIN iTNC 530 manual for 340 49x-03](https://content.heidenhain.de/doku/tnc_guide/pdf_files/iTNC530/34049x-neu/en/bhb.pdf)\n\nThe earlier Klartext prototype produced two programs for this installation. On the programming station running `606425 004 SP20`, both reached the end. The converter accepted 41 and 63 blocks. The station reached all three and five programmed stops. The physical machine still needs checks for the preset, quill position, retract clearance, drive state and coolant. This PR adds the machine data. The second PR supplies the writer and its golden programs.\n\n### Verification\n\nOn `7afbcbaf6`, the quick gate passed all 378 steps. The test logs recorded 2,963 passes. The focused run covered 106 tests. These included the 11 existing Heidenhain DIN/ISO goldens. Clippy passed for the touched app and post libraries and the machine-controller tests.\n\nThe new tests cover installation data at both post entry points, missing or additional axes, and the distinction between unknown and empty option lists. They also cover an invalid mixed machine input and a Picomax project that is saved and opened again. The full heavy gate passed all 199 steps. It recorded 43 release test passes, including all six 3D finish bands. The gate classified the pre-existing expected failures under its existing rules.\n\nPriority: P4, as on #3181.\n\nChangelog: Machine definitions can record the installed control, NC software, options and tool-change procedure. The catalogue includes the Fehlmann Picomax 55 with an iTNC 530.\n\nRefs #3098\n\nFixes #3181\n",
